{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From the fruit of the garden's trees we eat.</b> And we have no need to enter the danger of eating what the blessed El has told us will bring death upon us if we eat of it. Yet the imagination strengthened to ascribe jealousy and falsehood, heaven forbid, to the blessed El — portraying Him as having forbidden that fruit so that they would not attain the benefit of becoming <b>like Elohim</b>, and as though it would not cause death at all. And accordingly she said to the woman:"], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:46.612016005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}